  "ruledOutDirections": [
    {
      "id": "ruled-out-f371c48c9fb4",
      "text": "Measuring the in-process handler against the tracked database: the copy plus the copied generation file is what makes `readAdvisorStatus` report `live`, and it keeps every scratch write inside the lineage. Without the generation file the status read `absent` and the handler returned zero recommendations. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/freshness/generation.ts:47]",
      "contentHash": "f371c48c9fb4",
      "addedAtIteration": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ruled-out-1e32b3e57b7c",
      "text": "None this iteration. The first scratch run returned zero recommendations because the generation file was missing; copying it fixed the status read and is recorded under Ruled Out rather than treated as a dead end.",
      "contentHash": "1e32b3e57b7c",
      "addedAtIteration": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ruled-out-f65d95ad31b0",
      "text": "Timing the warm set on the same prompts used for warm-up: the prompt cache is keyed on prompt text and source signature, so a warm-up call would have filled the measured cache entry. Warm-up used two rows outside the measured set. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:602]",
      "contentHash": "f65d95ad31b0",
      "addedAtIteration": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ruled-out-0ea567ade5a0",
      "text": "None this iteration.",
      "contentHash": "0ea567ade5a0",
      "addedAtIteration": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "ruled-out-4fa22110dc85",
      "text": "Reporting the synthetic hub prompts as corpus rows. They exist only for the label check, and their ids carry the `synthetic-` prefix in every artifact.",
      "contentHash": "4fa22110dc85",
      "addedAtIteration": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "ruled-out-9ac0150495ad",
      "text": "Treating `degradedRecommendations` as drop-in compatible with handler rows. It re-derives a command from `commandRowFor(entry.skill)`, so a hub's attached command never survives and a typed command is lost. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1495]",
      "contentHash": "9ac0150495ad",
      "addedAtIteration": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "ruled-out-708cd12d8fc9",
      "text": "Summing the separately measured medians (CLI startup, handler import, handler call) as if that were a measurement. The composed process run replaces the sum and is the number quoted for the budget.",
      "contentHash": "708cd12d8fc9",
      "addedAtIteration": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "ruled-out-a0af0f9120be",
      "text": "Treating the `--version` spawn as the CLI's import cost. The spawn includes Node boot; the in-process import is 3.85 ms, and both are reported separately. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/inprocess-timing-4/scratch/compose-proposed.jsonl]",
      "contentHash": "a0af0f9120be",
      "addedAtIteration": 3
    }
  ],
